`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"The benchmark review covers 18 checked groups, one documented reproduction blocker, four unknowns and two explicitly unreviewed groups. It corrects an unsupported SWE-Game paper/catalogue association: similarly named resources with different task populations cannot establish one another's release. OpenGameEval's paper expressly describes its private session driver/system prompt and text-only observation condition. Those published limitations are kept separate from untested live-service behavior. WebGameBench quality rates are conditional on valid labels and require a separate coverage denominator; JAMER's offline model-generated configuration and inconsistent printed BAS dimension count remain explicit limitations. Recovered OpenGameEval source pins do not pin its private hosted service."}),`
